    "reason": "Active pull requests own shared governance, Wayfinder catalogs, Android Herdr, and Windows machine-profile surfaces. This harness composes with them without stealing their files."
  },
  "proofCeiling": "Tracked contracts, deterministic command-envelope rejection, corrected profile-transition envelope generation, cross-platform Python validation, Windows-native harness entrypoint shape, and hosted CI. It does not prove WSL is healthy, /bin/bash exists on an operator laptop, Termux is running on a phone, Herdr runs on Android, a provider responds, or an operator command completed."
